@0    = ~You look like a person who gets around! I need someone willing to conduct a small investigation for me. My... my loved one is missing, and I can't leave my post. Would you be willing to search for her? It's not far; just a quick look around in the city's northeast to see whether anyone knows where she went.~
@1    = ~Tell me more.~
@2    = ~No, I don't have time for that.~
@3    = ~Are you sure? You could just ask about her the next time you're near the Ilmater shrine by the Blushing Mermaid.~
@4    = ~Fine, tell me more.~
@5    = ~Blushing Mermaid? Well, if you'll reward me so that I can afford a visit inside as well—why not.~
@6    = ~I said no. You need to look for someone else.~
@7    = ~Dang. It's not that important, I'm sure she's just helping the poor somewhere, as she usually does. Anyway, I need to resume my rounds.~
@8    = ~Oh, and I think the Seatower commander is looking for you. Something about one of our prisoners who wants to talk to you. You'd best go to the commander's office; it's on the tower's second floor.~
@9    = ~Her name is Martina, and she is a monk of the Ilmater Monastery here in the tower. You see, the captain doesn't approve of in-tower liaisons; it's not against any official rules, but we all know he despises mingling among tower folk. So I have to keep this quiet. I already reported her missing, and the commander already sent a comrade to investigate, so anything I can do without deserting my post is done. I need an outsider to help.~
@10   = ~So, apparently Martina was seen at the Ilmater Shrine in northeast Baldur's Gate before she left again, but that's now also over two weeks ago! The abbot thinks it's nothing uncommon and doesn't see a need for another search party. I know that Martina helps the poor wherever she finds them and that her duties as a monk of Ilmater mean that she will stay and help wherever she sees people in need. It wouldn't be the first time that this has caused her absence for weeks at a time without notice. But this time it's been too long without any message to me, which is unlike her.~
@11   = ~I am quite desperate to hear any news. If you'd just go to the Ilmater shrine in the northeast of town and ask about her whereabouts and whether she was seen after we searched for her, I would be really grateful. I will give you a magical necklace I won at last year's sparring contest.~
@12   = ~I'll do it.~
@13   = ~Thank you! Please let me know as soon as possible what you find out. I'll be around... Not that I have a choice in the matter, haha.~
@14   = ~Thank you for looking into Martina's whereabouts. Let me know as soon as you know anything!~
@15   = ~Martina met a soldier on the first day of her rounds. This wasn't you, I presume?~
@16   = ~Something came up. On her rounds to spread the alms, a beggar saw Martina go behind the Ilmater shrine, and a soldier of the Watch followed her in a suspicious manner.~
@17   = ~Well, someone is lying. The beggar who saw Martina with a soldier the day she started giving alms, you about not seeing her since she left, or that partner you mentioned who also said he didn't see her that day.~
@18   = ~I'm on it.~
@19   = ~Hello! I finally got a day off and could come look for myself. One of the beggars said he last saw her coming here, with a soldier of the Seatower guard, no less? From what he said, this must have been my comrade, but... Is... is this... Martina?!~
@20   = ~Lenard, I am very sorry. This seems to be Martina.~
@21   = ~You tell me.~
@22   = ~Who else would it be?~
@23   = ~She... she is... No... no, please, no...~
@24   = ~I... I feared as much, but I was hoping... Thank... thank you for finding her for me. Here is the necklace, as promised... I will take her back to the monastery and will report my comrade's suspicious involvement. Why would he...? *sigh* Come by the tower again; I am sure the abbot would like to talk to you, and maybe the Seatower commander, as well.~
@25   = ~A... a soldier of the Watch was with her? This is the day my comrade said he couldn't find her! This doesn't add up. Now I'm getting a really bad feeling.~
@26   = ~He is on errands for the captain outside of the tower currently, so I can't make him explain himself. Please, as pointless as it seems, go and see whether you can find any more clues around the Ilmater shrine. Gods, how I wish I could leave my post!~
@27   = ~Please, if you will, good <SIRMAAM>. Spare a coin?~
@28   = ~I'm looking for a monk of Ilmater who goes by the name Martina. Have you seen her lately?~
@29   = ~Sure, here you go.~
@30   = ~Not now.~
@31   = ~Martina? I know her all right, but I haven't seen her for quite a while. I wasn't here at the shrine until last week, though. Maybe ask others of my kind, as we do switch places from time to time.~
@32   = ~Thank you very much, kind <LADYLORD>!~
@33   = ~Farewell.~
@34   = ~Hello! You wouldn't mind parting with a coin or two?~
@35   = ~Thank you for your generosity!~
@36   = ~Good day.~
@37   = ~I know her; she's a good soul. She comes by at irregular intervals and gives coins to all of us. She says her rounds need to be irregular or we would rely on them too much, may the gods bless her. I haven't seen her for weeks, though. I was at the palace the last three weeks, and my comrade Blurt was here at the shrine, in case that matters. He's at the palace now, in case you want to ask him too.~
@38   = ~What a shame to hear about Martina. I surely hope they'll get the bastard who did this!~
@39   = ~Ah, it's you again. Thank you for helping to get that bastard who killed Martina! Poor gal, she was such a good woman.~
@40   = ~Greetings, good <LADYLORD>. Could ye spare but a bit of change?~
@41   = ~Thank ye so much!~
@42   = ~Good day to you.~
@43   = ~Funny you'd ask about her. Two weeks ago, when I was begging in front of the Shrine of Ilmater, a soldier of the Seatower came asking about her, too. Turns out she spent more time collecting alms for the poor than anticipated and they got worried at the tower's monastery about her whereabouts. Well, she came back with the gold, and I got my coin; may the gods bless her.~
@44   = ~I guess the soldier was her loved one she always talks about, since I saw them going behind Ilmater's shrine shortly afterwards, heh.~
@45   = ~They went behind the shrine? Together?~
@46   = ~Wait a minute. It was not her lover who came to investigate for her, as far as I know.~
@47   = ~And this helps me how?~
@48   = ~Well, not "together" together, but close enough for me to notice! Though it could have been a coincidence, now that I think of it.~
@49   = ~Now that I think about it, I only saw Lenard later on when he was looking for her. I just assumed that the soldier who was with her earlier at the shrine was her lover. I'm beginning to wonder why the soldier spent so much time behind the shrine. I wonder what he was doing... maybe sleeping off a hangover? Heh. I haven't seen Martina since she handed out alms that day. Then again, I wasn't expecting to see her come around again anytime soon.~
@50   = ~Your friends at the shrine say that they haven't received alms from Martina in a while now.~
@51   = ~Thank you for your help.~
@52   = ~Sorry, it's all I can tell you.~
@53   = ~You mean Lime? He didn't get any alms from Martina when she visited? I didn't know that. Now that is odd. After handing out alms in front of the shrine, she usually does her rounds here at the palace. So even with talking to that soldier lad she should have been by the palace not much later. She must have skipped going here that day. Well, her rounds are at irregular intervals. Now I'm glad I was at the shrine that day!~
@54   = ~Either that or something happened. Have a good day.~
@55   = ~Oh, that would be a shame, really. Martina is such a nice person. I surely hope she's all right.~
@56   = ~Have a good day, good <SIRMAAM>.~
@57   = ~And I wouldn't mind a spare coin for my efforts, heh.~
@58   = ~You found Martina. May the gods have mercy. I can't believe she was buried there all this time. The poor gal.~
@59   = ~We heard about Martina's murderer. May he rot in prison for all I care! To think I thought it was her loved one who snuck up on her... The world is an evil place.~

/* crossmod with JAP */
@250 = ~I do know my sister Martina, but I wasn't here the last time she visited. You'd best ask one of the poor souls who are around the shrine. They are the ones she seeks out when she is here.~
